                <pb facs="0373" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg273"/>

                <head>No. 171.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 10, 1880</date>.
                        (Received August 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 704.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No 555, with which
                    I transmitted to you a copy of a circular addressed by me to our consular
                    officers in China, asking for information upon the war power of China as
                    indicated in their respective districts, I have now the honor to hand to you
                    copies of the responses which have been received. These include reports from all
                    our officers, except Mr. Shepard, at Hankow, and embody much interesting
                    information upon the subject.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD.</signed></closer>









